--- MODEL OUTPUT ---
The void folds inward. A low table of dark wood materializes before you, its surface scarred by candle scorch. Three cards lie face-down in a neat row. Your fingertips move without permission.

First card flips. Temperance. An angel pours liquid gold between two cups, wings brushing your pulse. Warm equilibrium floods your chest, as if someone adjusted the temperature of your blood.

Second card. Ace of Wands. A sprig of living flame grows from a wooden hand. Heat snaps against your knuckles, smelling of cedar kindling. Your heartbeat quickens, eager.

Third card. Two of Pentacles. A youth juggles copper coins in an endless loop. Your ankles remember balance; your shoulders feel the subtle tug of counterweight shifting.

These cards are now yours. They hum in your memory.

The table dissolves. The void tears like wet paper, and the Broken Lantern Inn rushes back in—woodsmoke, sour ale, the low murmur of late-night dice. You stand between tables, palm still tingling from the last image. Night presses against the shuttered windows.

